  "notes": "Cash basis city: one governmental fund (General Fund; Statement of Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balance p4, balance sheet p3) and one proprietary fund (Combined Utilities Fund, accrual statements pp5-7; measure net position), as in FY2023. Business-type receipts/disbursements from the proprietary Statement of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p6); no transfers printed for the utility fund. Business-type receipts total from the p8 Combined Utilities column (3,315,445 = 3,262,340 + 47,091 + 6,014). Governmental beginning cash not printed (no prior-year balance sheet); ending cash = Cash in Bank + Cash at County Treasurer (p3), investments 880,003 separate; fund balance roll-forward 573,472 - 232,183 = 341,289. Transfers out to the component unit (Statement of Activities p2 component unit 161,686). Proprietary cash flows (p7) include loan proceeds 2,945,330 and bond principal payments 229,835; proprietary null as in later years. Balance sheet: governmental lines from the governmental funds balance sheet (p3, ties to the Statement of Net Position governmental column 341,289; p1 prints the 880,003 as Restricted Investments / Restricted - Other Purposes, p3 as Investments / Assigned), business-type lines and totals from the Statement of Net Position (p1). Detail: the all-funds Budgetary Comparison Schedule (p8) by fund column; budget is printed only for the Totals column so budget_final is null. Read pages 1-8 of 8"
